From 2b946fb4aff77b2607a1720ddb22e96b67ce0e40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Campolo <campolo.alex@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:07:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] views: Add CefDisplayObserver

Applications that follow monitors being plugged in or switched on have
to poll CefDisplay::GetAllDisplays(): Chromium learns of a new output
asynchronously, so right after an output is switched on the list does
not have it yet (measured on Wayland with labwc: about 220 ms), and a
window sent to that display before it is listed ends up on another one.

Add CefDisplayObserver (OnDisplayAdded, OnDisplayRemoved,
OnDisplayMetricsChanged) and CefDisplay::AddObserver/RemoveObserver
(experimental API), a thin wrapper of display::DisplayObserver. The
adapter uses display::ScopedOptionalDisplayObserver, which does nothing
once the display::Screen is gone at shutdown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
